@1 = ~Oh, a new customer. Want a treato? I have lots of treatos! And magics. And junks I finds. Don't worry, I only takes junk from the dead. I is nice.~
@2 = ~Kobold on a Carnival?~
@3 = ~How often do you loot corpses?~
@4 = ~Show me your wares.~
@5 = ~What is wrongs about that? Me name Popper. Popper The Kobold. Me nothing like most of my kin.~
@6 = ~Lots of times! A baby wyvern ate a kiddo the other day. He had some goood stuffs. Ehm… uh, I means, 'Carnival is safe. No monsters around. Do not a-worry.'~
@7 = ~That will be all for now.~
@8 = ~Potion of Clear Consiousness~
@9 = ~Boots of NightCrawler~
@10 = ~Gloves 'Beautification'~
@11 = ~A potion with a sharp, briny taste. It grants temporary immunity to psionics and the mental assaults of mind flayers.~
@12 = ~Nightcrawlers were undead serpent-like beasts from the Plane of Shadows. Their chitinous armor was solid enough material to preserve some of the creature's powers. Although magic is nearly completely drained, the boots are functional by cloaking the wearer in an invisible mist that hides their presence and allows them to step into the shadows more easily.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Hide in Shadows: +30
- Set Traps: +10~
@13 = ~These gloves earned their reputation for being a show-stealer for anyone who wears them. Though their origin is unknown, they are imbued with nymph magic which transforms people of low charm into much higher standards. The recipient becomes persuasive, charming and more desirable no matter their earlier position. Only a handful of copies of this particular item have been reported, and each within 528,000 feet of Baldur's Gate city. Whoever created and distributed these gloves is likely situated in that area.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Charisma: +5~
